result: Verified the `?>` error-propagation operator is fully implemented end-to-end
  and conformant to docs/error-effects.md §4/§6. Lexer produces Token::QuestionGt
  (src/lexer/mod.rs:428); parser desugars postfix `?>` to a match{Ok(v)?v; Err(e)?!e}
  via pending_propagates/wrap_propagates (src/parser/expr/pratt.rs, src/parser/stmt/mod.rs);
  typer/From-trait conversion applies E.from(e) on the err arm across layers; `!`
  early-return retained and unchanged. All 12 conformance tests in tests/error_effects.rs
  pass, including propagate_converts_via_from_across_layers (multi-layer From conversion),
  propagate_early_exits_on_err, propagate_on_option_returns_nothing, and propagate_outside_fallible_fn_is_error.
  Build is zero-warning. The `! E` sugar form (`returns i64 ! FileError`) wrapping
  into Result is deferred to 2-4 (note added) — `?>` itself is complete with the canonical
  `Result of T,E` form.
description: 'Implement the ?> error-propagation operator (distinct from overloaded
  ?). SPEC: docs/error-effects.md §4 (parse postfix ?>, desugar to match{Ok(v)?v;
  Err(e)?! E.from(e)}) and §6 (From trait conversion). Retain ! for explicit early
  return. Done when read(path)?> propagates and converts via From end-to-end.'
